{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cassert>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\ntypedef vector< vector< int > > mt;\n\nmt shift(const mt &a, int shift)\n{\n    int k = int(a.size()) - 1;\n    shift = (k - shift) % k;\n    mt res = a;\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < k; ++j) {\n            res[i][j] = a[(i + shift) % k][(j + shift) % k];\n        }\n    }\n    for (int j = 0; j < k; ++j) {\n        res[k][j] = a[k][(j + shift) % k];\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nmt operator *(const mt &a, const mt &b)\n{\n    int n = int(a.size()), k = int(a[0].size()), m = int(b[0].size());\n    mt res(n, vector< int >(m, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n            int tmp = 0;\n            for (int l = 0; l < k; ++l) {\n                tmp = (tmp + 1ll * a[i][l] * b[l][j]) % MOD;\n            }\n            res[i][j] = tmp;\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    ll n;\n    int k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    int max_depth = 0;\n    {\n        ll tmp = n;\n        while (tmp != 0) {\n            ++max_depth;\n            tmp /= k;\n        }\n    }\n    vector<mt> dp(max_depth);\n    dp[0].assign(k + 1, vector< int >(k + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j) {\n            dp[0][i][j] = (i == j || j == 0);\n        }\n    }\n    mt e(k + 1, vector< int >(k + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        e[i][i] = 1;\n    }\n    // Different DP construction: use while loop over bits of k\n    for (int depth = 1; depth < max_depth; ++depth) {\n        dp[depth] = e;\n        mt bs = dp[depth - 1];\n        int curx = k;\n        int bit = 0;\n        while (curx > 0) {\n            if (curx & 1) {\n                dp[depth] = bs * shift(dp[depth], (1 << bit));\n            }\n            curx >>= 1;\n            if (curx > 0) {\n                bs = bs * shift(bs, (1 << bit));\n            }\n            ++bit;\n        }\n    }\n    mt base(1, vector< int >(k + 1, 0));\n    base[0][k] = 1;\n    int sl = 0;\n    ll x = n;\n    vector<int> vec;\n    while (x != 0) {\n        vec.push_back(x % k);\n        x /= k;\n    }\n    int len = int(vec.size());\n    for (int cur_depth = len - 1; cur_depth >= 0; --cur_depth) {\n        int rest = vec[cur_depth];\n        for (int it = 0; it < rest; ++it, sl = (sl + 1) % k) {\n            base = base * shift(dp[cur_depth], sl);\n        }\n    }\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        res = (res + base[0][i]) % MOD;\n    }\n    cout << res << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    static int[][] shift(int[][] a, int shift) {\n        int k = a.length - 1;\n        shift = (k - shift) % k;\n        int[][] res = new int[a.length][a[0].length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n            System.arraycopy(a[i], 0, res[i], 0, a[i].length);\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n                res[i][j] = a[(i + shift) % k][(j + shift) % k];\n            }\n        }\n        for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n            res[k][j] = a[k][(j + shift) % k];\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int[][] multiply(int[][] a, int[][] b) {\n        int n = a.length;\n        int k = a[0].length;\n        int m = b[0].length;\n        int[][] res = new int[n][m];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n                long tmp = 0;\n                for (int l = 0; l < k; l++) {\n                    tmp = (tmp + (long) a[i][l] * b[l][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n                res[i][j] = (int) tmp;\n            }\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int[][] copy(int[][] a) {\n        int n = a.length;\n        int m = a[0].length;\n        int[][] res = new int[n][m];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            System.arraycopy(a[i], 0, res[i], 0, m);\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n\n        int maxDepth = 0;\n        long tmp = n;\n        while (tmp != 0) {\n            maxDepth++;\n            tmp /= k;\n        }\n\n        List<int[][]> dp = new ArrayList<>(maxDepth);\n        int[][] first = new int[k + 1][k + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= k; j++) {\n                first[i][j] = (i == j || j == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n            }\n        }\n        dp.add(first);\n\n        int[][] e = new int[k + 1][k + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {\n            e[i][i] = 1;\n        }\n\n        for (int depth = 1; depth < maxDepth; depth++) {\n            int[][] cur = copy(e);\n            int[][] bs = dp.get(depth - 1);\n            int curx = k;\n            int bit = 0;\n            while (curx > 0) {\n                if ((curx & 1) != 0) {\n                    cur = multiply(bs, shift(cur, 1 << bit));\n                }\n                curx >>= 1;\n                if (curx > 0) {\n                    bs = multiply(bs, shift(bs, 1 << bit));\n                }\n                bit++;\n            }\n            dp.add(cur);\n        }\n\n        int[][] base = new int[1][k + 1];\n        base[0][k] = 1;\n\n        List<Integer> vec = new ArrayList<>();\n        long x = n;\n        while (x != 0) {\n            vec.add((int) (x % k));\n            x /= k;\n        }\n\n        int sl = 0;\n        int len = vec.size();\n        for (int curDepth = len - 1; curDepth >= 0; curDepth--) {\n            int rest = vec.get(curDepth);\n            for (int it = 0; it < rest; it++, sl = (sl + 1) % k) {\n                base = multiply(base, shift(dp.get(curDepth), sl));\n            }\n        }\n\n        int res = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {\n            res = (res + base[0][i]) % MOD;\n        }\n        System.out.println(res);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, -1.6093124941107817e-05, -1.7881233361549675e-05, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.16695962846279144, -1.7881233361549675e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.015979677438735962, -0.0024786246940493584, -1.847726889536716e-05, -0.01841425895690918, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006715585943311453, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.026317980140447617, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.023792358115315437, -3.933898824470816e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00037865620106458664, -2.50339189733495e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.006400680169463158, -0.00650751544162631, -1.19